        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Moe Greene, Moe Dalitz, Hyman Martin\n- Works: The Godfather\n- Places: Pittsburgh\n- Roles: fictional character, gangster, businessman, casino owner, philanthropist, mobster\n\nFacts:\n- Morris Barney Dalitz, known as Moe Dalitz, was born on December 25, 1899, and became an American gangster, businessman, casino owner, and philanthropist.\n- Hyman \"Pittsburgh Hymie\" Martin was born on April 6, 1903, and was a Pittsburgh mobster.\n- Morris \"Moe\" Greene is a fictional character who appears in Mario Puzo's 1969 novel The Godfather.\n- Morris \"Moe\" Greene also appears in the 1972 film adaptation of The Godfather.\n- Hyman Martin was a close associate of Moe Dalitz and Louis Rothkopf.\n- Hyman Martin died in July 1987.\n- Moe Dalitz died on August 31, 1989.",
